cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'qmath: A research library for quantitative finance'
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arias Gomez
    given-names: Alejandro
    email: aleexariasg@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/aleexarias/qmath'
abstract: |
  qmath is a research library for quantitative finance. It provides typed,
  tested implementations of pricing models, volatility-surface fits, and
  option-implied estimators behind a small and consistent API, so that methods
  from different families can be composed and compared on the same data. The
  first area built out is option-implied risk-neutral density recovery.
keywords:
  - quantitative-finance
  - options
  - derivatives-pricing
  - volatility-surface
  - density-estimation
  - risk-neutral
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 0.1.0
